      ],
      "content": "SP 8707               WENDOVER               HALE ROAD west side 11/234                                       Winterton House II Home for the Elderly, formerly the Vicarage. 1871-3 by George Devey. Red brick with diaper patterns in blue brick, irregular plinth of sarsen stone. Tiled roof, picturesque composition with many gables moulded brick eaves. 2 storeys and attic, lst floor band. Entrance on N. front, lean-to porch in recess with 2-light casement to LH, 3-light above. Gable to RH has large projecting chimney stack with offsets and 2 diagonal shafts. Gable to LH has canted oriel to 1st floor, 2-light casements to ground floor and attic. Lower service wing to LH, altered. Garden (W) elevation has narrow gable to LH with dentil verge small panel in tympanum, 4-light window with moulded head to 1st floor, 4-light transomed window to ground floor. Large chimney stack in centre, now taken down to eaves level, square bay to RH with french window. Listing NGR: SP8711207661"
    }
  ],
